WEBVTT

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.100
A cultural festival, huh?

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.060
Guess it's that time of year.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.570
We have tests coming up.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.990
It's such a pain how we have to do so much in second semester.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.990
That's all you have to say...

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.370
...heading into our last cultural festival of high school?

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.370
Opening ceremony?

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.040
What's this?

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.330
Every year...

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.960
...during the Outou Festival...

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.460
...groups of people perform at the beginning of the day.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.010
<i>I just had a great idea!</i>

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:35.970
Now then...

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.300
Our class has decided...

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.680
...to host a fortune telling house for the festival...

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.810
...so please come up with your own method of fortune telling...

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.400
...before our next homeroom.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.540
You worked hard!

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.480
I was touched!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.180
And so...

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.650
I'm thinking about doing a cheerleading routine!

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:54.700
Cheerleading?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.570
For the opening ceremony we talked about this morning.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:02.300
It would be the best performance to pump up the festival.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.500
It does sound flashy and fun.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.620
Doesn't it?

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.750
We'll be the talk of the town!

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.420
B-By we, you mean...

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.920
We're part of it?

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.470
I asked the teacher...

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:20.140
...and was told that the plan must be
properly developed which requires members.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:25.890
Wh-What about you, Yutaka?

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.690
M-Me?

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.360
It might be physically hard on Yu-chan.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.240
Maybe I should give it a try.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.110
I guess I might try if it isn't any trouble...

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.490
Trouble?

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.780
Absolutely not!

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.830
You're very welcome!

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.710
W-Will you be okay?

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.250
It'll probably be hard...

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.630
...so I might just hold everyone back...

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.300
...but I'd like to give it a try this time.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:53.920
There!

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.510
Yutaka's willing to do it.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:57.840
What do you two say?

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.560
In that case...

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.430
Well, if everyone's doing it...

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.100
I have wonderful friends!

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.440
Fortune telling, huh?

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.570
But do you even know how to tell fortunes?

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.110
Not a clue.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:14.860
<i>Holy cow...</i>

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:15.610
Hey!

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.900
Wasn't it your idea?

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.530
You can just wing it when it's for a cultural festival.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:22.620
That's right...

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.750
What's your class doing, Sis?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:26.580
Well...

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.170
We're being generic and going the haunted house route.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.790
A classic, huh?

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:35.050
We couldn't come up with any other fun ideas.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.130
Something wrong?

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.170
Nah.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.470
I just thought it was very appropriate...

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.930
What are you trying to say?!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.390
The real-life demon's angry!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.970
Knew you would say that...

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.100
And so...

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.890
Patty-chan said she wanted to do cheerleading.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.400
So...

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.650
I thought I might work hard at it.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.570
Why?

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.530
I'm always absent...

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.820
...so I never accomplished anything with other people.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.490
But I'm feeling better these days.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.290
What I've been wanting to do...

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.620
...and what Patty-chan wants to do right now...

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.790
...might be the same thing, you know?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.460
But it'll be pretty rough...

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.800
And...

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.880
We don't have enough people...

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.930
...so Patty-chan was wondering if you could participate.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:23.970
So that's how it goes...

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.310
You're good at sports...

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.680
If people like you and Minami-chan are there...

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.850
...I might be able to hang in there to the end.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:37.230
I can tell that you're really serious about
this, and Patty's also asking me for help...

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.240
Yes?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.320
Hello?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.610
Good evening!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.820
Konata!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.990
It's Patty, huh?

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.950
I just heard about your idea and was thinking it over...

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.000
Time for a quiz!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.750
I'm holding a certain ticket in my hand right now.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.540
Well...

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.840
What do you think the ticket is for?

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.470
C-Could it be...

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.640
Konata.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.760
You loved the Jam, didn't you?

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.560
Don't you want to exchange a hot handshake with Haruhi?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.850
Handshake session!

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.310
I wanna go! I wanna go!

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.310
Aya in the flesh!

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.610
By the way, Konata...
Aya in the flesh!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.230
...weren't you about to say something?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.860
Yu-chan.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.200
Let's work hard to make some memories!

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.910
Which means...

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.870
This is the age of cheerleading, girls.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.620
What kind of reasoning is that?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:37.590
Patty came up with the idea of doing a cheerleading
routine during the cultural festival's opening ceremony.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.750
Sounds fitting enough.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.380
Which is why the two of you will also be dancing.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.510
Are there any other people in your class who can dance, Kagami?

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.100
H-Hold it right there!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.470
Don't just go on ahead without our permission!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.600
I-I probably can't do that stuff...

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.190
But we probably won't get another chance like this.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.020
It's a once-in-a-lifetime chance.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.110
We'll be doing it with people we know.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.030
Plus, it's a festival.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.570
It's more fun if we go crazy with everyone.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:08.990
Really?

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.540
You might be right!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.960
You're so easily convinced...

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.290
I refuse.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.960
I have to prepare for my class project.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.930
I just wanted to make some memories
during our last cultural festival together...

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.890
You always bring up friendship out of nowhere!

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.300
It's obviously an act!

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:35.770
Yu-chan's really pumped up about this.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.150
But will she be okay?

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.530
I told her she shouldn't do it...

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:47.660
But she was really earnest about wanting to accomplish something with everyone.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.820
R-Really...

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:49.700
But you know...

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.660
She said that they don't have enough people.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.080
That's how I got involved.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.830
I guess I was a little forceful about it.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.500
I shouldn't push people into this.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.550
I'll just ask someone else.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.090
Fine...

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.840
What?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.180
Fine!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.260
I'll do it!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.970
Sis!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.720
Really?

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.520
I can't help it.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.560
My class can just replace me with someone else...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.060
...but you guys can't do that.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.480
<i>Kagami sure is cute.</i>

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.860
Ch-Cheerleading, is it?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.780
I'm not confident I'd do a good job...

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:28.950
Well...

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.530
We're not too sure about a lot of things right now...

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.330
<i>Especially in terms of volume.</i>

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.370
I'd feel a lot better if you joined us!

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.370
Is that so?

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:42.840
I understand.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.050
If I can be of help...

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.720
Thanks, Boin—

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:48.760
I mean, Miyuki-san...

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.890
Testing is over...

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.350
...so we'll be focusing on preparations for the cultural festival...

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.100
...but don't get too relaxed!

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.180
Honestly...

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.150
They could cut down on testing when we have school events...

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.730
Yo!

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.150
Hey, Konata.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.110
What's going on with the cheerleading thing?

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:07.990
That reminds me...

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.610
Before testing started...

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.530
"They approved the plan!"

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.160
...is what I heard...

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.740
But I haven't heard anything since.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:15.660
What?!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.040
How irresponsible!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.250
We're not gonna have enough time to practice at this rate...

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:19.870
Or actually...

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.870
It's already too late!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.250
Guess we'll go ask.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.670
Sorry!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.170
I haven't worked out the choreography yet!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.710
Haven't worked out the choreography?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.050
What are we supposed to do then?!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.430
It's also taking time to pick a song.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.760
It's not easy to find something on Sunny Sunshiny's level.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:37.520
What was that?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.270
Anyway...

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.350
If you were having trouble...

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:46.190
...you should have asked other people for help.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.440
This was your idea...

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.030
...so you need to be responsible for scheduling!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.860
So many difficult Japanese words I don't know!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.910
How can you say that when
you've done perfectly fine up until now?!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.790
At least get some of the choreography done today!

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:01.500
We'll work out the kinks as we practice!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.250
Ask someone who's free if you can't figure something out!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.800
Miyuki and I can handle general
scheduling and reserving a practice location!

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:09.880
We're counting on you!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.970
Kagami...

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.800
You were pretty against this idea...

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.300
...but like...

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.810
...you're the most passionate one here.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:21.390
Be quiet!

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.890
What are you going to do, Miyuki-san?

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.520
I'll be using tarot cards.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.530
And what about you, Tsukasa?

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.990
I haven't decided yet...

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.360
Yuki-chan.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.820
Is there something even I could do?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:38.620
Let's see...

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.330
How about one that involves reading shapes?

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.300
Th-This shape...

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.260
...means that your love fortune is good...

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.720
...m-most likely!

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.970
Tsukasa.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.640
You just made that up, didn't you?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.890
Y-Ya think so?

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.230
W-Wait a second!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.020
You want us to learn this?!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.570
It's no good?

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.280
It's not an issue of quality...

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.690
It looks fairly difficult.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.860
We don't have much time.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.660
Shouldn't we just simplify the harder parts as we go?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.790
Holy cow...

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.910
But if we get through this...

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.080
...a wonderful feeling of satisfaction awaits us!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.370
You shouldn't be saying that!

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.540
We're out of tape.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:30.880
It can't be helped.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.880
I'll make a trip to the store.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.970
Then grab magic markers while you're at it.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.380
And some exacto refills.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.220
Cardboard!

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.220
Playboy.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:38.930
Glue.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.350
Something weird got mixed up in there...

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.680
And if we need to buy so much stuff...

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.890
...stop playing around and go buy it!

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.060
What are we calling the fried soba?

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.730
Breath of Fragrant Spring.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.820
What's this Fallen Drop of Sunlight?

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.240
That's Japizza.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:56.990
Man...

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.570
You can't tell what's what on this menu!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.080
Japanese culture is so fun.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.870
This project seems to be abusing stereotypes...

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.120
Hey!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.040
What are you guys doing?

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.040
Um...

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:12.130
A-A Zuka cafe.
Um...

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.090
A-A Zuka cafe.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.630
Wh-Wh—

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.420
What is this?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.590
Basically...

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.640
It's a cafe where you can enjoy shows in the spirit of Zuka.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.640
With girls in shiny dresses...

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.100
...and beautiful girls in male clothing...

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.140
...serving as waitresses.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:28.980
Two for one!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:29.810
Male clothing...?
Two for one!

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.150
That's right!

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.610
Yu-chan and Minami-chan are the leads!

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.280
In their dazzling, beautiful world!

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.610
When was this decided...

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:41.370
I'm also worried about the cheerleading...

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.950
...but is this going to work?

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:47.080
Those two are something else.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.210
You're very good, Minami-san.
Those two are something else.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:49.250
Then let's try it again.
Those two are something else.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.040
They sure are.
Then let's try it again.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:51.630
And they're perfectly in rhythm.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.880
Okay!
And they're perfectly in rhythm.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:52.960
And they're perfectly in rhythm.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.210
By the way...

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.800
Would that be considered sadistic on the part of Miyuki-san...

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.220
...or masochistic on the part of Minami-chan?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:00.970
When you put it that way...

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.300
Takara-senpai's dynamic dance moves...

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.600
...are probably putting pressure on Minami-chan.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.100
Ya think so?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.980
Just forget that and practice.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.110
The cheerleading costumes are complete!

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.240
It looks great!

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.280
It looks wonderful...

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.490
...but it's a bit embarrassing.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:26.160
These kinds of costumes make the people watching happier.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.370
In fact...

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.620
...this outfit was chosen by one of those who like to watch.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.750
The one you mentioned last time...

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.840
The dreadful, older Tamura brother.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.340
You can expect some great Zuka costumes, too!

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.050
That's right...

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.420
You guys are doing a cheerleading routine?

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.810
Can I take pictures?!

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.680
Within reasonable limits.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:52.600
I'll be careful...

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.270
Well...

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.150
We haven't done it successfully yet...

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.980
...so we're pretty worried.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.820
I'll use my power to charge you up...

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.240
...so work hard!

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.320
Your power...

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:07.370
...might charge us up so much we tire ourselves out.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.200
Basically like that.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.370
It's pretty rough considering how we have no time left.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.370
A cultural festival, huh?

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:16.540
What did we do for ours?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.550
We had what you now call...

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.210
...you know...

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.550
...a manga cafe.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.260
All the boys in our class...

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.840
...brought in their manga.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.890
So you guys were ahead of your time.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.680
It may seem normal to bring manga nowadays...

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.190
...but back when we were in school, they were strict about it.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.940
You could only do it during festivals.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.980
Well, people bring it to school...

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.400
...but it's not really approved...

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.490
A fortune telling house, is it?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.950
Let everyone know...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.280
...to give me a good fortune if I come.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.200
B-But that wouldn't be fortune telling...

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.800
By the way...

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:56.080
How was it when you were in school?

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:01.300
I think each class or club had their own project.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.920
The projects were stuff like haunted houses...

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.470
...and Japizza vendors...

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.260
Mostly standard fare.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.140
It's rather strange how...

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.560
...it doesn't seem much has changed.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:13.810
By the way...

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:17.100
...was a study of a cultural item such as Paulownia cabinets...

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.730
...ever used as a project?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.610
What's that?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.900
That wouldn't be any fun at all, now would it?

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.320
You're right...

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:27.530
Absolutely right...

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:28.910
Okay!

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.620
Time for a break!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.250
It looks like we can pull off an exciting performance.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.000
Well...

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.170
It's not complete yet...

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.050
So hang in there to the very end.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.010
This is when...

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:46.130
...it's a big help to have Hiiragi here to take command.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:47.510
Well...

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.640
I don't want to be the only one left out of the memory.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:52.810
Wh-What is it?!

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:53.680
Don't stare at me!

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.230
My...

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.640
Is that so?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.610
I'm terribly sorry about that.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.820
No trouble at all.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.200
It appears that today's a rehearsal...

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.120
...and only students are allowed.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:10.660
So?

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.740
We, the general public...

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.870
...can't get in until tomorrow.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.790
That's why I told you to check before coming here!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.170
But...

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:25.090
I heard that Akira-chan would be here today.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:25.670
Geez!

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.050
What a waste of train fare!

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.510
If we still had that money...

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.300
...we could have had hamburger steak or something fancy!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.550
Yeah...

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.890
I really dig this feeling of incompleteness.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.230
Leave us alone.

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:37.060
And, like...

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.980
...you're walking around in that?

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.940
This serves as advertising.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.900
Your costume's cute, Kona-chan!

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.070
Gotta start from the appearance.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.490
I'll read lots of fortunes today!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.160
In five minutes and fifteen
seconds, you will buy soft-serve ice cream...

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.540
At five minutes and twenty-eight
seconds, you will drop it on your leg.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.790
Fortune telling doesn't mean to predict the future.
At seven minutes and six seconds, you will hit your head on a sign.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.710
Word for word?!
At seven minutes and six seconds, you will hit your head on a sign.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.750
You guys look great.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:02.420
But...

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.790
...we're just as good!

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.800
It took till the very last second...

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.010
...but we're finally done!

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:11.970
So cute!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.890
You look wonderful.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.560
It's really embarrassing to walk around in this costume...

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.270
That's some outfit...

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.310
Oh, but it's cute.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:22.400
Chief.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.230
Akira Kogami's about to go on stage.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.020
Really...

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:27.190
I'll be right there.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.030
Nice to meet you, Teacher.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.450
I'm Akira Kogami!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.200
I'll work hard today!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.370
Sakuraba.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.330
I'm.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.580
Today's like a rehearsal...

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.080
...so we'll just be running some check-ups...

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.170
Countin' on you.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.080
Hey, Shiraishi.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:45.380
You handle the rest.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.670
Yes.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:49.460
I'm the cultural festival planning committee chair, Shiraishi.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.090
It's a pleasure.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.930
I'm letting Shiraishi handle the rest...

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:56.010
...so let him know if you need something.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.350
Please.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.220
Okay!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.400
Hey, you.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.520
Say something.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.690
You should have gone to the demon council.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.240
Something wrong?

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:10.690
Is?
Something wrong?

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.910
No, nothing's wrong!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:13.950
We were going through things...

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.870
...and got a little too excited!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:22.250
Anyway...

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:24.330
You're an appreciated guest...

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.630
...so we'll treat you accordingly.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.010
So?

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.170
After this...

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:35.590
...we'll need a mic check for Cape of Thirty Years on Lucky Channel.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.850
Feel free to say whatever you
want after the song onstage tomorrow.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.810
Well, I'll do a good job of it.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:41.430
Then...

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:44.060
Please head to the stage.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.440
Damn Shiraishi...

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.610
Weak...

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:48.940
Good lucky!

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.570
Thank you for coming to see Akira, everyone!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.410
I hope you have lots of fun today!

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.700
She longs to be in the arms of her beloved...

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.450
Will such a day ever come?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:05.000
As she drifts alone...

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.920
...guided by his words from that day...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.500
She'll go anywhere in search of a trace...

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.920
Here's a song.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.220
Akira Kogami-san with...

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.470
Cape of Thirty Years.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.010
Would you mi—

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.180
Okay, that's enough!

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.270
Goddamn it!

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:22.430
Let me sing my song!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.890
I told you it was just a check!

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.020
We don't have time!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.400
Like I give a damn!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.940
So many difficult Japanese words I don't know!
I'm going to kill you, bastard!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.570
Is everybody ready?

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.530
This is the last run-through.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.700
I came up with this idea a little spontaneously...

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:44.160
...but the fact that I've been given a
chance to do something with everyone...

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.210
...makes me really happy.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:47.960
Instead of worrying about success or failure...

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.460
...I just think we should have fun!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.520
We did it!

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.230
It's like, holy cow.

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:32.440
Ya think so?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.610
What's this?
Ya think so?

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.320
You're still here?

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.610
We were practicing our cheerleading routine.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:38.400
Really.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.110
So how's it going?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.160
Can't wait to see it.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.240
Teacher!

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.910
I'm thirsty!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.790
Guess it's okay.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.910
I suppose I can buy drinks for hardworking young people.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.210
Lucky!

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:54.710
Is it really okay?

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.090
Sure thing.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:57.840
This is a special case though.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.090
In return...

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.130
...be sure to make the first event at the festival...

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:01.970
...a real blast!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.430
Okay!

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.640
What's up, Tsukasa?

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:15.860
How should I put it...

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.320
It kinda feels strange.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.030
That's right.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.320
Actually...

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.110
...I'm also feeling a bit melancholic.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:28.950
They say you have the most fun when preparing for a festival.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.200
That's right...

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.250
Tomorrow's the real thing.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.370
That's right.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:37.630
We may never stay at school so late again.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.290
You feel a bit lonely when you look at it that way.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.140
Ta-Tamura-san...

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.770
Your face is really strained.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:52.980
Yeah...

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:53.810
Like...

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:55.020
My stomach hurts...

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:55.690
Tsukasa...

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.480
You're frozen stiff, aren't you?

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:01.070
You don't look so calm yourself.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:06.160
B-Being nervous helps you concentrate!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:10.200
I think I'm so nervous I can't move.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:10.910
Test. Test.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:14.750
Then we will now begin the Outou Festival!

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.080
The first performance today...

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.420
...was submitted by a foreign student, Patricia-san.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.590
A cheerleading routine performed by a group of friends.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.840
Then let's begin...

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:25.590
U-Uh, sorry.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.380
Cell phones should...

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:26.800
It's mine!

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:27.760
Crap!

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.730
Running into trouble at the very end!

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:36.520
That relaxed me so much I almost fell!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.900
Great timing!

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.150
Wasn't that guy so lame?

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:42.320
They say that trouble tends to follow people around.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.860
Well, I guess this is appropriate for us.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:48.910
How we can never be serious, huh?

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:49.870
Okay, well...

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.330
Y'know...

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.160
Yes!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:52.910
Sorry about that!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.960
I'm really sorry!

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:55.710
Okay!

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:58.040
Then let's try that again!

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.130
Take it! Sailor Uniform!
